::CW_U06_L02_GP_Q01::Author statement: "I guess this poem is fine, and people can think whatever." What is the main tone problem?{
~A. It is too specific and reflective.#Incorrect. The statement is not specific or reflective.
~B. It explains too much craft reasoning.#Incorrect. It gives almost no craft reasoning.
=C. It sounds uncertain and dismissive.#Correct. The tone does not fit a publication-ready author statement.
~D. It is too organized.#Incorrect. The statement lacks clear organization.
}

::CW_U06_L02_GP_Q02::Which author statement sentence has the strongest tone?{
=A. I revised this piece to make the speaker's uncertainty clearer through repeated images.#Correct. The tone is reflective, specific, and publication-ready.
~B. This is good and nobody should question it.#Incorrect. This sounds defensive and exaggerated.
~C. I wrote stuff and it happened.#Incorrect. This is vague and careless.
~D. People probably will not get it.#Incorrect. This sounds dismissive rather than reflective.
}

::CW_U06_L02_GP_Q03::Which order best organizes an author statement?{
~A. Complaint, plot summary, random detail, apology.#Incorrect. This does not support craft reasoning.
~B. Font, file name, page number, favorite color.#Incorrect. This does not explain the creative work.
~C. Summary only, with no craft reasoning.#Incorrect. An author statement should do more than summarize.
=D. Purpose, craft choices, revision or growth, reader effect.#Correct. This order keeps the statement focused and useful.
}

::CW_U06_L02_GP_Q04::Which revision improves defensive language? Original: "If people do not understand the ending, that is their problem."{
~A. My ending is perfect and everyone else is wrong.#Incorrect. This remains defensive.
=B. I used an open ending so readers could feel the speaker's uncertainty rather than receive a simple answer.#Correct. This replaces defensiveness with craft reasoning.
~C. I do not care about readers.#Incorrect. This is still dismissive.
~D. The ending exists.#Incorrect. This does not explain purpose or effect.
}

::CW_U06_L02_GP_Q05::Which statement best fits a publication context?{
~A. This piece is random and I did not revise it.#Incorrect. This weakens credibility and gives no craft reasoning.
~B. Nobody should ask me about my choices.#Incorrect. This is defensive.
=C. I removed extra explanation so the final image could create a quieter ending.#Correct. This is reflective, specific, and appropriate.
~D. It is good because I said so.#Incorrect. This is unsupported.
}
